      <div className="bg-slate-100 p-8 rounded-xl my-8 text-sm leading-relaxed border-l-4 border-crimson">
        If any person in the nighttime enters without breaking, or in the daytime breaks and enters or enters and breaks, the dwelling house of another, with intent to commit murder, rape, robbery or arson, he shall be deemed guilty of burglary.
      </div>

      <h2 className="text-3xl font-serif text-navy mt-16">§ 18.2-90 & § 18.2-91 — Statutory Burglary</h2>
      <div className="bg-slate-100 p-8 rounded-xl my-8 text-sm leading-relaxed border-l-4 border-crimson">
        Any person who, in the daytime or nighttime, breaks and enters or enters and breaks any office, shop, storehouse, warehouse, or any other building or structure with intent to commit larceny, or any felony other than murder, rape, robbery or arson, shall be deemed guilty of statutory burglary.
      </div>

      <h2 className="text-3xl font-serif text-navy mt-16">Penalties</h2>
      <ul className="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-lg">
